COMMENTS.COMMENT:
These states bypass the normal action-record animation: 7 = Block Stun 8 = Critical Stun 9 = Hit Stun F = Down-Attack Stun In those states, ACT_CODE becomes a reaction code.
The resolver uses: g_character_reaction_record_tables @ 0x00099450 g_common_reaction_records @ 0x0009BDB0 Each reaction record is 0x10 bytes.
Codes 0x30–0xB7 select the shared reaction table: record = &g_common_reaction_records[action_code - 0x30];
Codes outside that interval select a character-specific reaction table. Codes above 0xB7 are remapped: reaction_index = (action_code + 0x78) & 0xFF;

branches on Kasumi, Leifang, Tina, and costume number
selector = player_index + resource_set[player_index] * 3;
/* * Configures and queues a costume-dependent auxiliary resource for * Kasumi, Leifang, and Tina. * * Builds a device-side transfer descriptor using a player/resource-set * slot selected by FUN_00062F90. Skipping this routine prevents resource * completion and can leave the character invisible while the main CPU * waits. * * Female-only behavior makes a relationship to chi/breast data plausible, * but this is not the per-frame physics updater and the association remains * unconfirmed. */

Animation pointer-bank directory. Bank = anime_id >> 9;
local entry = anime_id & 0x1FF. Character-ID holes generally use
Zack's bank as fallback. Read by Motion_Initialize at 0x0004e500

